# The Gorani release key (commit 39g, docs/INSTALL.md › Checking a download).
#
# verify.sh / verify.ps1 accept a release only if SHA256SUMS.sig was made by
# a key listed here, for the principal "release@gorani" and the namespace
# "gorani-release" — one line per key:
#
#   release@gorani namespaces="gorani-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAA… gorani release key
#
# The release manager makes the key on their own machine — never in CI — a
# hardware key if they have one:
#
#   ssh-keygen -t ed25519-sk -f ~/.ssh/gorani-release -C "gorani release key"
#
# and adds its .pub here with the prefix above. Until a line is here, every
# release is refused. Whoever installs compares the fingerprint verify
# prints with the one the release manager gave them in person — a key read
# from the same place as the download proves nothing on its own.
